&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MasterClass is &lt;em&gt;the &lt;/em&gt;platform where the world’s best come together so anyone, anywhere, can access and be inspired by their knowledge and stories. We put you in the room with the creators, thinkers, makers and leaders who have changed the world, so that you can change yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MasterClass Executive is our selective, cohort-based program for senior professionals learning to lead in the AI era, taught by world-class operators and academics in collaboration with the University of Chicago Booth School of Business and OpenAI.&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;Admission is competitive: applications are reviewed individually, and spots in each cohort are limited.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring an Admissions Advisor as a temporary, full-time employee to support our next enrollment cycle. You&#39;ll spend most of your day on the phone and in the inbox with applicants and admitted candidates — answering questions about the program experience, helping them weigh the value of enrolling, and guiding them from admission to enrollment ahead of cohort deadlines. You&#39;ll also support employer-sponsored enrollment: equipping candidates to make the case to their company and responding to inquiries from managers, HR, and L&amp;amp;D teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-volume, goal-driven role during our busiest enrollment windows. The ideal candidate is a natural on the phone — consultative, warm, and credible with senior professionals — and genuinely fluent in both AI and the business-education landscape. You know what programs like ours cost, what the alternatives promise, and how to have an honest conversation about fit and value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a high volume of admissions calls — scheduled consultations and proactive outreach with applicants and admitted candidates — answering questions about the curriculum, live sessions, AI Labs, in-person intensive, time commitment, and cohort experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help prospective enrollees evaluate the program&#39;s value: speak confidently and accurately to outcomes, program fees, and payment options, and position MasterClass Executive honestly against the alternatives candidates are weighing (executive education, MBA programs, certificates, and cohort-based courses)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide admitted candidates from decision to enrollment with timely phone and email follow-up through each enrollment window, identifying and removing blockers before deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run point on employer-sponsorship communications: respond to sponsorship inquiries, provide candidates with materials to secure company support (manager emails, ROI summaries, program overviews), and flag multi-enrollee company interest to our partnerships team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage your pipeline with clean notes and reliable follow-through; meet daily and weekly contact and response-time goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Log the questions, objections, and sponsorship themes you hear and share them weekly with the admissions and marketing teams to sharpen FAQs, call guides, and email copy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide surge coverage during peak moments: post-webinar follow-up, enrollment-deadline outreach, and inbox support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in admissions or enrollment advising, inside sales, account management, or another phone-forward consultative role — executive education, higher ed, edtech, or premium consumer experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuinely energized by phone time: you listen first, handle objections without a hard sell, and are comfortable with 20–30+ meaningful conversations a day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong writer who can run a high-volume inbox with responses that are crisp, warm, and never read like a template&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversant in AI: you follow the space, use the tools yourself, and can speak credibly with senior professionals about how AI is changing their work (no technical background required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and able to navigate uncertainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in the business-education landscape — executive education, online MBAs, certificates, and cohort-based programs — and how buyers compare them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and self-directed: strong CRM hygiene, pipeline discipline, and comfort being measured against clear goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable in a fast-moving environment where call guides, offers, and priorities evolve week to week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available across U.S. time zones, including some early-evening hours when candidates are most reachable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Details:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Temporary, full-time employment via our staffing partner TCW Global with an anticipated initial assignment of approximately one month; MasterClass may extend the assignment in its discretion based on cohort needs and business demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employment is at will; nothing in this posting guarantees employment for any specific period or any extension of the assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote (U.S.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Temporary, Full-time, ~40 hours/week, nonexempt (overtime eligible)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pay: $28-$34/hour base pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benefits: The selected candidate will be employed through our third-party staffing partner, TargetCW, and is not eligible for MasterClass employee benefits (including health insurance, paid time off, and retirement plans). Sick leave and other benefits required by applicable law will be managed directly by TargetCW.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At MasterClass, we believe we put our best work forward when our employees bring together ideas that are diverse in thought. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state or local law. In addition, MasterClass will provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities.&amp;nbsp; If you have a disability or special need, we would like to know how we can better accommodate you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MasterClass is the streaming platform where the world&#39;s best come together so anyone, anywhere, can access and be inspired by their knowledge and stories. We put you in the room with the creators, thinkers, makers and leaders who have changed the world, so that you can change yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Members get unprecedented access to 200+ instructors and classes across a wide variety of fields, including Arts &amp;amp; Entertainment, Business, Design &amp;amp; Style, Sports &amp;amp; Gaming, Writing and more. Step into Nas&#39; recording studio and Gordon Ramsay&#39;s kitchen, and go behind the big screen with James Cameron. Design your career with Elaine Welteroth, get ready to win with Lewis Hamilton, perfect your pitch with Shonda Rhimes and discover your inner negotiator with Chris Voss.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to help make an impact on our members&#39; lives – we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are looking for more than what a resume can show. If you don&#39;t have the exact experience or skills, but think you&#39;d be a great addition to MasterClass, please apply for the role.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;freelance&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;AI Project Reviewer, you will be responsible for evaluating learner submissions against detailed rubrics for a new product. You will apply consistent judgment to determine pass/fail outcomes and provide clear, constructive feedback to help learners improve. Working alongside our product and learning design teams, you’ll help calibrate and validate assessment approaches to ensure fair, accurate, and valuable feedback for our members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a temporary role with flexible engagement based on project needs. ~20 hours per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and evaluate projects against detailed rubrics, providing consistent pass/fail judgments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear, actionable feedback that helps learners understand areas for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the learning design and product team to refine rubrics and assessment criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compare human and AI assessment outcomes to identify areas for calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document reasoning behind evaluation decisions to support assessment consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in assessment, evaluation, or educational feedback roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to consistently apply detailed rubrics across multiple submissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication skills with the ability to articulate reasoning clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing constructive feedback to support learner growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while maintaining high standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to refrain from using AI during evaluations and written rationales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in roles such as Mentor or Coach in educational settings, Educational Evaluator or Teaching Assistant (TA), Consultant in AI or learning design, or Instructor with experience in grading and providing feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’re a Great Fit If You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about education and committed to helping learners succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a keen eye for detail and take pride in maintaining high standards in evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy collaborating with cross-functional teams to enhance assessment quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable making nuanced judgments while ensuring consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working independently and managing your time efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are curious and open to learning more about AI-driven evaluation methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;body body--medium&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hourly Range: $75-$125 USD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;body body--medium&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;The hourly range listed is for NYC/CA/WA. As a company, we have a location based strategy, which means the disclosed range estimate has not been adjusted for any applicable geographic differential associated with the location where the position may be filled.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;body body--medium&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At MasterClass, we believe we put our best work forward when our employees bring together ideas that are diverse in thought. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state or local law. In addition, MasterClass will provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. If you have a disability or special need, we would like to know how we can better accommodate you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MasterClass is the streaming platform where the world&#39;s best come together so anyone, anywhere, can access and be inspired by their knowledge and stories. We put you in the room with the creators, thinkers, makers, and leaders who have changed the world so you can change yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Members get unprecedented access to 200+ instructors and classes across various fields, including Arts &amp;amp; Entertainment, Business, Design &amp;amp; Style, Leadership, Writing, and more. Step into Issa Rae’s writing session and Gordon Ramsay&#39;s kitchen. Go behind the big screen with James Cameron. Start your career with Martha Stewart.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Creative Director to shape the creative and brand strategy for MasterClass Certificates and lead its execution across the business. You will bring individual Certificates to market in fresh, compelling ways while helping evolve how the broader offering is positioned as the product grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be a creative lead on the marketing team, working directly with our Executive Creative Director to shape how MasterClass Certificates show up in the world. You&#39;ll work alongside a small, close-knit team assembled around each project. This is a hybrid role: part strategist, part maker. You&#39;ll help position and launch one of MasterClass’ newest products by getting close to the work and leading a nimble team made up of editors, designers and writers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have creative authority, a seat with senior stakeholders, and the trust to make calls fast, often with incomplete information. Success here comes from building alignment across teams and earning trust through strong campaigns, concepts and execution. At its core, this role is about finding the strongest idea and helping it become something people can&#39;t ignore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape creative strategy and lead execution&lt;/strong&gt; for MasterClass Certificates. Concept and oversee work across trailers, course promos, statics, social, lifecycle marketing, product storytelling, and executive presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help define and evolve the Certificates brand. &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with the GM, Product Marketing, Product, and GTM leads to translate changes in the product and business model into clear positioning, messaging, identity, and creative expression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead creative direction&lt;/strong&gt; on trailers, from identifying on-set capture needs through final edit. Dream up video content that pulls audiences toward a course, including ideas beyond the traditional trailer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roll up your sleeves&lt;/strong&gt; when it counts. Write scripts and copy, shape a rough layout or edit, build your own decks, and stay close to the work, not just directing it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set and hold the creative bar&lt;/strong&gt; for Certificates marketing. Lead video, design, and copy creative with clear direction on the idea, tone, message, and craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect the work&lt;/strong&gt; across Content, Social, and Product. Partner with the teams shooting the classes, creating organic content, and building the product to ensure the creative reflects real audience needs, not just a marketing brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI is part of your process. &lt;/strong&gt;Use AI to accelerate ideation, exploration, and production without sacrificing brand voice, originality, or craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Present with authority. &lt;/strong&gt;Pitch creative strategy and rationale to senior leadership and hold the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A brand builder who can move between positioning a product, defining how a business shows up, and turning that strategy into creative people recognize and want.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural leader who rallies teams around a creative direction without formal authority over them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at translating strategy into a clear creative point of view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A creative with strong taste and original thinking that still sells&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable directing editors, designers, and writers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to turn a product pitch into a story someone actually wants to hear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in using AI as part of your process, not as a separate step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident making calls with 80% of the information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast without sacrificing judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Energized by cross-functional work and able to turn multiple perspectives into focused action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct and discerning, raising the work without deflating the people making it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–12 years of experience in creative roles, ideally including both agency and in-house environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that shows both strategic range and hands-on craft, not just direction of others&#39; work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building or evolving brands across positioning, messaging, identity, campaigns, and product experience, not simply maintaining an established system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting creative strategy directly to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading through matrixed or project-based team structures rather than direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency with AI creative tools in an active production workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Versatility across copy, visual and art direction, video/trailer direction, and executive presentation materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At MasterClass, we believe we put our best work forward when our employees bring together ideas that are diverse in thought. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state or local law. In addition, MasterClass will provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. If you have a disability or special need, we would like to know how we can better accommodate you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The salary range listed is for NYC/CA/WA. As a company, we have a location based strategy, which means the disclosed range estimate has not been adjusted for any applicable geographic differential associated with the location where the position may be filled.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;MasterClass’s salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry. In addition to salary, we also offer equity and comprehensive benefits (medical, dental, vision, flexible PTO, and more). The range listed is for the expectations as laid out in the job description, however we are often open to a wide variety of profiles, and recognize that the person we hire may be less experienced (or more senior) than this job description as posted. If that ends up being the case, the updated salary range will be communicated with you as a candidate.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$165,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$190,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
